A||N||3||terryk||Dash/Gauge Ground Miswired?||||5||
Z||000000||terryk||09-23-2001||03:44 PM||||Somewhere I remember someone commenting about the dash or gauge ground circuit being mis-wired (poorly chosen might be a better phrase) which causes the gauges to change with the load on the alternator and battery.<P>I was thinking about it and reading the wiring of the gauges. Something's amiss at the Circle K.<P>Anyone know something about this?<P>Terry<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Steve Normington||09-23-2001||06:52 PM||||If the ground on the connector to the right (as you look at it on the car) is not well connected, the gages behave erratically. I believe it is wire #11 (the connector is numbered).||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-23-2001||07:30 PM||||Check the stuff in the wire service article in my cave. Specifically check the thin ground from the battery to the body and the one from the head to the body.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||09-23-2001||08:37 PM||||I've checked them all and they are good and tight and no corrosion.||||reg||1
